//? Title: Brute-Force Path Search: Incumbents, Pruning and Factorial Work
//? Subtitle: Actual simple-path visits, minimum-edge ties and an explicit-stack native search
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given a directed unweighted graph, find a start-to-goal path with the fewest
edges. Backtracking can solve this by exploring simple path prefixes, but
many prefixes can reach the same vertex and the search can require factorial
work. This implementation retains the shortest path found so far and prunes
prefixes that cannot improve it. We inspect that actual search, retain the
original three-vertex chain, and verify a closed-form dense unreachable case.
The canonical native loop supplies the paths, visit records, bounds and counts.
)

\toc

> A worked graph: a long incumbent, a shorter replacement and a tie

Start at zero and seek five. Input order first follows 0→1→2→5, a three-edge
path. The edge 2→0 is rejected because zero is already on that live path.
The next root branch finds 0→3→5, which has two edges and replaces the
incumbent. The last root branch first reaches prefix 0→4→1. That prefix
already has three vertices, as many as the incumbent, and is cut off.
Path 0→4→5 also has two edges; a strict-improvement tie rule retains 0→3→5.

The graph highlights the returned path in green. The table lists the two
actual incumbent changes; it does not reconstruct them using another search.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/brute_force_incumbents.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t,std::size_t>> edges{{0,1},{1,2},{2,0},{2,5},{0,3},{3,5},{0,4},{4,1},{4,5}};
  const auto trace=dm::algorithms::brute_force_search_trace(6,edges,0,5);
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint> position{{0,0},{3,2},{6,2},{4.5,0},{3,-2},{9,0}};
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(75,1100);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;style.circle=true;style.width=.8;style.height=.8;style.padding=7;
  for (std::size_t v=0;v<position.size();++v) {
    const bool selected=std::find(trace.result.path.begin(),trace.result.path.end(),v)!=trace.result.path.end();
    style.fill=selected?dm::RGB{220,252,231}:dm::RGB{219,234,254};
    diagram.node(std::format("v{}",v),position[v],std::format("{}",v),style);
  }
  for (const auto& [u,v]:edges) {
    bool selected=false;
    for (std::size_t i=1;i<trace.result.path.size();++i)
      if (trace.result.path[i-1]==u && trace.result.path[i]==v) selected=true;
    dm::graphics::DiagramStroke stroke;stroke.color=selected?dm::RGB{22,163,74}:dm::RGB{148,163,184};
    stroke.width=selected?3:2;
    diagram.edge(std::format("v{}",u),std::format("v{}",v),"",stroke);
  }
  diagram.text({4.5,3.5},"DFS tries the route through one before the route through three")
      .text({4.5,-3.4},std::format("returned path: {}; {} edges",trace.result.path,trace.result.path.size()-1))
      .save_svg("build/brute_force_incumbents.svg");
  std::print("| visit | new incumbent | vertices | edges |\n| ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (const auto& row:trace.steps) if (row.improved)
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",row.id,row.path,row.path.size(),row.depth);
  std::print("\nFinal path: {}; entered prefixes: {}; cycle rejections: {}; bound prunes: {}.\n",
      trace.result.path,trace.result.expanded,trace.cycle_rejections,trace.bound_prunes);
}
```
