\caption(The visit budget counts entered prefixes, not unique vertices. A positive limit throws before an excess visit; zero means unlimited. It limits search visits rather than graph allocation and returns no partial result.)

> A factorial family: dense reachable component, isolated goal

Place the start in a complete directed graph on k vertices and leave goal k
isolated in a graph of k+1 vertices. No incumbent can be found, so no length
bound activates. Every ordered subset of the k−1 other reachable vertices is
a simple prefix from the start. The exact number of entered prefixes is

$$
V_k=\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}\frac{(k-1)!}{(k-1-j)!},\qquad
V_1=1,\qquad V_k=1+(k-1)V_{k-1}.
$$

Every visited endpoint has k−1 outgoing arcs and all are scanned. Hence
A_k=(k−1)V_k, with A_k−V_k+1 rejected cycle arcs. The native generator supplies
all directed non-loop arcs within the component. A trace without prefix copies
measures this search, while BFS exhausts only k vertices on the same input.
The table and figure compare these different logical visit events, not runtimes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/brute_force_factorial_visits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> component,dfs_log,fifo_log;
  std::size_t expected=1;
  std::print("| component k | actual DFS prefix visits | factorial-sum reference | inspected arcs | (k-1)*V_k | cycle rejections | BFS dequeues |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (std::size_t k=1;k<=9;++k) {
    if (k>1) expected=1+(k-1)*expected;
    const auto edges=dm::algorithms::complete_directed_graph_edges(k);
    const auto trace=dm::algorithms::brute_force_search_trace(k+1,edges,0,k,{0,false});
    const auto fifo=dm::algorithms::breadth_first_search_trace(k+1,edges,0,k);
    if (trace.result.found || fifo.result.found || trace.result.expanded!=expected ||
        trace.edges_examined!=(k-1)*expected || trace.cycle_rejections!=trace.edges_examined-expected+1 ||
        fifo.result.order.size()!=k) return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",k,trace.result.expanded,expected,
        trace.edges_examined,(k-1)*expected,trace.cycle_rejections,fifo.result.order.size());
    component.push_back(k);dfs_log.push_back(std::log10(double(trace.result.expanded)));
    fifo_log.push_back(std::log10(double(fifo.result.order.size())));
  }
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create().lines(component,dfs_log,"DFS prefixes",dm::RGB{37,99,235},2)
      .points(component,dfs_log,"",dm::RGB{37,99,235},4)
      .lines(component,fifo_log,"BFS dequeues",dm::RGB{22,163,74},2)
      .points(component,fifo_log,"",dm::RGB{22,163,74},4)
      .title("Isolated goal: factorially many DFS prefixes")
      .x_label("vertices k in the reachable complete directed component").y_label("log10(actual visit count)")
      .y_limits(-.2,6.5).size(900,500).save_svg("build/brute_force_factorial_visits.svg");
}
```
